            <exercise workspace="2in">
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        Section 2.3: 2, 3, 4, 8 (look at examples for these!)
                    </p>
                    <p> Writing: with your partner, start a document that has the results from the box on page 120 as a theorem: <q>Theorem: For every <m>n \times n</m> matrix <m>A</m>, the following statements are equivalent:</q>. Use the <c>enumerate</c> environment to list the five equivalent statements. </p>
                    <program language="latex">
                    <code>
                    \begin{thm*}[The Big Theorem] 
                        For every $n \times n$ matrix $A$, 
                        the following statements are equivalent:
                            \begin{enumerate}
                                \item $A$ is nonsingular.
                                \item
                                \item 
                                \item 
                                \item 
                            \end{enumerate}
                    \end{thm*}
                    </code>
                    </program>
                </statement>
            </exercise>
        </worksheet>
